WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.233
[music]

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.166
[Instructor] We've set up our game now
so that our Score Text can

3
00:00:09.166 --> 00:00:12.600
actually use the score variable
that we have in our Game Manager.

4
00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:15.733
But it doesn't actually do anything so

5
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:20.100
we're going to add in ways
that we can actually update our "Score."

6
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:24.133
In our GameManager class

7
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.266
we're going to create another function
so that we can actually update

8
00:00:28.266 --> 00:00:31.766
our "score" and then update
our ScoreText.text accordingly.

9
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.766
If we create a new method

10
00:00:35.766 --> 00:00:39.800
we'll make this void for now,
since it's just calculating our score

11
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.000
and then updating something already.

12
00:00:42.466 --> 00:00:46.633
You don't need to return any values.
We'll call it "UpdateScore()."

13
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.366
And then in our UpdateScore()

14
00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:54.066
we're just going to take out
our scoreText.text

15
00:00:54.066 --> 00:00:56.066
where we update it here,

16
00:00:56.266 --> 00:00:59.033
cut it and paste it
into our UpdateScore().

17
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.166
Now every time we call UpdateScore()

18
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.466
it's just going to tell
us our current score

19
00:01:04.466 --> 00:01:06.500
which isn't really that useful

20
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.500
since our current score is 0,
and it's not actually doing anything.

21
00:01:09.733 --> 00:01:12.100
So we're going to use parameters here

22
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.900
so that we can actually
add to our score every time

23
00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:18.266
and then that way it'll
update the scoreText.text here.

24
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:24.100
So we'll use an integer
and call it "scoreToAdd."

25
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.733
So this will be the score that we add
into our current score every time.

26
00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:34.066
Now we need to actually
update the score itself

27
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.366
before we update the text
because that's what the text is using

28
00:01:37.366 --> 00:01:40.400
to actually change the score.
So if we type score

29
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.733
and then we say += scoreToAdd

30
00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:52.266
now it'll add whatever value
we pass into our parameter

31
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.166
on to our score because remember
this is the same as saying score

32
00:01:57.733 --> 00:02:02.700
is set to score plus scoreToAdd.
So the original score that we had

33
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.700
plus the value that we pass
in here so now it should UpdateScore().

34
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:11.433
So now if we go to our Start() method
we should say UpdateScore()

35
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.133
and we're not adding anything because
it's the first time it's running.

36
00:02:16.866 --> 00:02:20.500
So it should just tell us the score
which should just be 0 anyways.

37
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.933
So if we play our game
you should just see...0, cool.

38
00:02:26.566 --> 00:02:31.066
So we know that works.
We still need to update it.

39
00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.833
So I think a good place
to update our score

40
00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:41.800
in our Game Manager is probably
whenever we spawn a target.

41
00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:45.200
At least just for now,
just to see that it works.

42
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.833
So in here every time
we spawn a new enemy,

43
00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:51.400
will update our score...

44
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.066
I'll just say 5 every time.
So every time one of those blocks spawns

45
00:02:56.633 --> 00:02:58.700
it should just add 5 to our score.

46
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.333
So if we test this in our game...

47
00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.333
Cool. So every time
one of these blocks spawns

48
00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:13.233
it adds 5 to our
score every single time.

49
00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:17.266
So works for now.

50
00:03:18.366 --> 00:03:21.266
So what you're going to do
in your GameManager class

51
00:03:21.566 --> 00:03:24.933
is you're going to create 
your own UpdateScore() method

52
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.900
and pass in a parameter
for the scoreToAdd

53
00:03:29.466 --> 00:03:32.400
and then you're actually
going to use some calculations

54
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.833
so that we can take our current score

55
00:03:35.466 --> 00:03:38.533
and add in the scoreToAdd
on to it already.

56
00:03:39.666 --> 00:03:43.600
And then using the line of code
that we had in our Start() method before

57
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:48.633
we'll set our scoreText.text

58
00:03:48.633 --> 00:03:52.766
to be score concatenated with
the new score that we updated.

59
00:03:55.566 --> 00:03:58.666
Now when you start the game,
make sure you call UpdateScore(0)

60
00:03:59.166 --> 00:04:01.900
and just pass it a 0,
because we're not adding anything to it.

61
00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.033
And then just to test it out
in your Spawn Target Method,

62
00:04:06.866 --> 00:04:08.966
add an UpdateScore() Call

63
00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.500
and just pass it the number 5
so that when you play your game

64
00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.900
you should see it update too.
Now it's your turn.

65
